  "boundaries": [
    "Stages overlap; do not sum. All build failures and corrected boundaries are retained.",
    "The original owned BlueprintImplementation API retains its seven arguments and delegates to a shared creation transaction. A new additive primitive/string role accepts the selected registered contract receipt. This adds no external CELEM type or execution profile.",
    "Owned function creation observes the object, published function and root manifest. Registered creation observes only the two owned sources and independently re-reads the selected external function/manifest receipt. The external function is never added to editable ownership.",
    "The dedicated external contract reader loads only declaration files, with no provider body or final provider selection. The ordinary graph view later reads its owned node sources for preservation and diagnostics. A receipt fence is not a filesystem-wide atomic snapshot.",
    "Creation changes an existing object and root registration plus three new owned sources. The five required sources are one review group; other pending declarations sharing registration are explicitly included by the existing rules. Compiler Confirm remains separate from staging and Save/cold restore.",
    "Scaffold generation reuses only the function signature and a temporary intent. The real function, its default provider, parent objects/modules and original C# are preserved. The initial node source is empty with an unset definition stamp.",
    "The creator requires a published explicit function signature with no function parent. Same-function object-parent provider reuse remains complete; different-function implementation inheritance still uses the existing IMPLEMENTATION_ID diagnostic. Function-import wrapper creation, legacy conversion and extended graph/internal type profiles remain separate work.",
    "All execution uses owned local fixtures. Windows/Android managed gates compile only. No main/original ZIP/Android settings, real account, paid model or user PC installation changes."
  ],
